{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMurphy"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy.xComp_mul_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy.xComp_mul_σ","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMurphy.lean#L66-L71","doc":"The same on the right — `x_μ · σ_i = q · x_μ`, the two-sided statement Murphy's\n`m_{st} = T_{d(s)}^* x_μ T_{d(t)}` needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy.σ_mul_xComp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy.σ_mul_xComp","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMurphy.lean#L54-L64","doc":"**The eigenvector property, in the composition's own terms.**\n\n`σ_i · x_μ = q · x_μ` whenever `i` and `i+1` share a block of `μ` — i.e. for every\nsimple reflection *inside* a part, which is the generating set of `S_μ`.\n\nThe algebra is entirely `HeckeMurphy.σ_mul_murphySum_subgroup`; what this supplies is\nthe hypothesis in a form that can be checked from the parts of `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy.xComp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy.xComp","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMurphy.lean#L47-L52","doc":"**Murphy's `x_μ` for a composition**: the sum of `T_w` over the Young subgroup of\n`μ`.  For `μ` a partition this is the usual `x_λ`; the point is that it is defined\nwithout one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy.mem_youngOfComp_sw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy.mem_youngOfComp_sw","kind":"theorem","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionMurphy.lean#L26-L45","doc":"Membership of a **simple transposition** in a composition's Young subgroup is\nexactly the statement that the two labels it swaps share a block.\n\nThe reverse direction is where the content is: a transposition fixes the block\nfunction everywhere outside the two points it moves, so agreement at those two points\nis all that is needed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}